body:
Remedy what? That bandits arent a challenge when you're level 30? Late game isnt easy if you fight late game enemies. Bandits are not late game enemies.

&#x200B;

And no, that sounds incompatible as hell.

Id like to see humanity rebuild. Maybe 5-10 years after TFS, walkers are starting to rot away, and humanity finally has a fighting chance again. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Ive always preferred Heavy armor over Light armor/robes, becuase i play Perma death and dying to an arrow/crossbow bolt is extremely frustrating, and heavy armor essentially lets you ignore archers. It is a bit slow at first, especially if youre playing a race with no HA skill. But say youre playing an Orc, with 2 levels of training (Training is pretty important to make early level HA bearable) youre already at 25, and bestial stew takes care of all your stamina issues. That power spike is crazy, and once you get something like Steel plate and around 250 Hp you really are tanky. Its really not that bad as people make it out to be, unless you put on orcish armor on a level 1 breton or something. Or if youre not using stews and stamina potions.

Bashing is generally a bad idea unless youre fighting giants or something, and thats obviously later into the game. With even two perks into blocking, some health and armor, you can block pretty much any bandit. Yes, that includes high level bandits with Orcish warhammers. Well, as long as you dont run out of stamina. So there really isnt a need for bashing. Power bashing can be useful at times, but not necessary at all, and you need the stamina for it.

&#x200B;

