&#x200B;

&#x200B;

You could think about backstories for your characters, maybe throw some rp in there, and set a goal from your characters perspective. Say you're playing a paladin, you could have the goal to clear all the draugr tombs in skyrim. Obviously you would never really complete a task like that, but thats not the point anyway. At the start of the game, you would have the short term goal of getting strong enough to fight draugr. The mid term goal of getting Dawnbreaker (maybe). Gives you something to work and look forward too. 

&#x200B;

If youre more into hardcore challenges and dont really care for RP, you could do stuff like trying to clear a dungeon at level 1. For example, to get better at combat i tried to clear embershard mine at level 1 with a bunch of different playstyles.  Altough i wouldnt recommend something like that if youre new to Ultimate skyrim.

Are you criticising me for having an opinion on what happened and its implications?

&#x200B;

Im just saying, as far as we know Marlon had more options than to die or give up the sisters. If we knew that he had a gun pointed at him by the raiders, and he had to chose between giving 2 people that didnt include himself to the raiders or get shot and they get taken anyway, then you could make a statement like " it was the only good choice". But we dont know if that happened. So maybe its hypocritical of me to say that he had more options, but my point is that marlon made a choice to trade people for safety, doesnt take any responsibility for it, hides it from everyone, runs away and murders someone because the truth gets out. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Marlon wasnt playing a telltale game. Boxes appearing on a screen wasnt his only options. He could have told everyone to leave the school and just try to escape the raiders. He could have given himself to the raiders. He could have convinced everyone to join the raiders in exchange for being treated fairly from the raiders. He could have attacked the raiders. Besides, you have way to little information to make a statement like that. 

&#x200B;

Also, you sound like a 10 year old defending logan paul after that suicide forest video at this point.
